# Any models. Router mode: configuration lives in models.ini, not here.
#
# Router mode: model configuration lives in the INI, not here.
#
# This preset is deliberately empty. Anything set here becomes an environment
# variable on the router, which every model instance inherits — so a value here
# silently becomes a default under all of them, competing with the same key in
# your models.ini. One config layer is easier to reason about than two.
#
# Set context, thinking, offload and speculative decoding in the INI instead:
#   presets/globals.ini      global defaults for every model (the default)
#   examples/models.ini      per-model configuration
#
# The other presets/*.env files are for the single-model case, where you pass
# `-m /models/some-model.gguf` and there is no INI in play.
